epublican Ralph Alvarado, a former state senator with a health care background, faces Democrat Zach Dembo, an attorney who has matched Alvarado nearly dollar for dollar in fundraising.\n\nMost raters call the race Likely Republican, though a few say Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-four chance. Democratic-sponsored polls from August show a tied race, and outside groups tied to Governor Beshear and Trump-aligned PACs have poured money into the Lexington-area district. The evidence points to a modest Republican edge with real room for movement.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2515, "margin": -3.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.296, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2877, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2982, "margin": -4.0}]}